To configure the Huawei NE40E router to replace all private AS numbers in the AS_Path with the local AS number when advertising to peer group `CUSTOMER_EDGE`, follow these steps:

### 1. **Define an AS_Path Filter to Match Private AS Numbers**
Create an AS_Path filter that matches all private AS numbers (64512-65534 for 16-bit, 4200000000-4294967294 for 32-bit):
```bash
ip as-path-filter private_as_filter permit ".*(6459[0-4]|645[7-8][0-9]|6459[5-9]|64[6-9][0-9]{2}|65[0-4][0-9]{2}|655[0-2][0-9]|6553[0-4]|420000000[0-9]|42000000[1-9][0-9]|4200000[1-9][0-9]{2}|420000[1-9][0-9]{3}|42000[1-9][0-9]{4}|4200[1-9][0-9]{5}|420[1-9][0-9]{6}|42[1-9][0-9]{7}|4[3-9][0-9]{8}|[5-9][0-9]{9}|[1-3][0-9]{10}|4[0-1][0-9]{9}|42[0-8][0-9]{8}|429[0-3][0-9]{7}|4294[0-8][0-9]{6}|42949[0-5][0-9]{5}|429496[0-6][0-9]{4}|429497[0-2][0-9]{3}|4294973[0-8][0-9]{2}|42949739[0-3][0-9]|429497394).*"
```
**Explanation:**  
This complex regex matches any AS_Path containing private AS numbers in the specified ranges. Adjust if using a different private AS range.

### 2. **Create a Route Policy to Substitute Private AS Numbers**
Replace all private AS numbers in the AS_Path with the local AS number (e.g., `65001`):
```bash
route-policy REPLACE_PRIVATE_AS permit node 10
  if as-path-filter private_as_filter
  apply as-path substitute private-as
