{'Parameters': 'cbs cbs-value', 'Info': 'Specifies a committed burst size (CBS), which limits the maximum number of bytes available for a burst of packets in a short interval to remain within CIR.\nThe value ranges from 15000 to 1500000, in bytes. The default value is 15000.'}
{'Parameters': 'pir pir-value', 'Info': 'Specifies a peak information rate (PIR), that is, the peak rate at which packets can be transmitted or forwarded.\nThe value ranges from 12000 to 60000, in kbit/s. The default value is 48000.'}
