To configure the Huawei NE40E router's BGP-IPv6 unicast session to send routing updates to peer `2001:DB8:2::2` at a minimum interval of **20 seconds**, follow these steps:

### Step-by-Step Configuration:
```bash
# Enter BGP configuration mode
<HUAWEI> system-view
[HUAWEI] bgp {as-number}  # Replace {as-number} with your local AS

# Configure the BGP peer (if not already set)
[HUAWEI-bgp] peer 2001:DB8:2::2 as-number {remote-as}  # Replace {remote-as} with the peer's AS

# Enter IPv6 unicast address family view
[HUAWEI-bgp] ipv6-family unicast

# Set the minimum advertisement interval for the peer to 20 seconds
[HUAWEI-bgp-af-ipv6] peer 2001:DB8:2::2 min-advertisement-interval 20

# (Optional) If the peer isn't activated yet, enable it
[HUAWEI-bgp-af-ipv6] peer 2001:DB8:2::2 enable

# Save the configuration
[HUAWEI-bgp-af-ipv6] commit
[HUAWEI-bgp-af-ipv6] return
<HUAWEI> save
```

### Key Commands:
1. **`peer 2001:DB8:2::2 min-advertisement-interval 20`**  
